From 82a89bc50bbbbc679aaffcb016ca7dff0a409c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:26:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 045/202] Translations: clearer Japanese names in the File and
 Edit menus

"Revert" had the same Japanese name as "Undo"; it now says "back to
the saved state". The file commands speak of files instead of
"documents" like the start page, "Transform" says what it does (move
and turn), matching the context bar, and duplicating is just "duplicate".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
